ng here over the last decade  and the median price for a home of more  than 450 thousand dollars housing is an  immensely complex issue vanessa murphy  live local now  so the state is looking for business and  community partners to get affordable  housing projects going all across the  state pre-applications are being  accepted right now we have a link to  that and a link for renters and  homeowners that need help at  eightnewsnow.com  democratic assemblywoman pat spearman  she's a lot of things she's a retired  military policewoman a pastor a musician  and a doctor has a doctorate in business  administration well now she wants to add  north las vegas mayor to that resume i  spoke with her this week about her  campaign  why run for mayor  running for mayor gets me closer to the  people  i believe we've done a lot of good  things in carson city at the state level  to enhance people's lives  to make things better  but once the governor signs those bills  it's almost impossible to know if all of  them have been implemented or even if  they've been  implemented correctly so what this does  is it gives me a chance to take the  knowledge the experience and the  relationships that i have at the state  senate and bring them a lot closer to  the people and make sure that i'm doing  the right thing that makes people's  lives comfortable having that positive  impact we've got to diversify our  economy you know our economy is such  that when las vegas catches a cold north  las vegas gets pneumonia because we  don't have all of the beautiful trinkets  that they do at the uh down on the strip  and so i want to diversify our economy i  have a doctorate in business  administration and my uh assuming my  dissertation has been downloaded almost  a thousand times on every continent in  the world  in europe alone it's close to 200 times  and i talk about sustainable development  and talk about renewable energy that was  what my research was on and so i want to  look at renewable energy