on from our  washington dc bureau alex let's talk  about the details of president biden's  announcement regarding trying to  regulate these ghost guns  hey there well it was really interesting  to watch this announcement you know  president biden in the rose garden with  a with ghost guns it's not something  that you see every day and it was really  playing into the messaging that  president biden and the biden  administration  are trying to convey and really his  overall message  in that announcement was that ghost guns  are real guns they're equally as  dangerous and equally as deadly as a gun  that you would purchase you know already  put together president biden announced  this final rule on ghost guns it does a  few different things but  most importantly what it does is that it  prohibits businesses from manufacturing  ghost gun kits without serial numbers  that will belong to those guns and it  also prohibits gun dealers from selling  the ghost gun kits  without doing proper background checks  like they would have to do if they were  selling a  an already assembled gun  to any purchaser so that's the  president's proposal about dealing with  ghost guns what's the reaction on  capitol hill from republicans  well we've already heard senator ted  cruz leading an effort for example with  a couple of other senators announcing  new legislation to try to push back and  stop the biden administration from  enforcing this new rule on ghost guns  and i want to read you part of the  statement that senator cruz released he  said  we're pushing back we want to stop the  biden administration from issuing the  final rule expanding the definition of  firearms and instituting a national gun  registry so that is how senator cruz is  kind of characterizing the action that  the biden administration um is taking  and that was alex limon from washington  dc we do expect gun groups like the nra  to file lawsuits as soon as the order is  actually put in place  well lake mead is at its